This is covered in the R Installation and Administration Manual in Appendix A:

  http://cran.r-project.org/doc/manuals/R-admin.html#Essential-and-useful-other-programs-under-Unix

"Unless you do not want to view graphs on-screen you need ?X11? installed, including its headers and client libraries. For recent Fedora distributions it means (at least) ?libX11?, ?libX11-devel?, ?libXt? and ?libXt-devel?."

HTH,

Marc Schwartz


